<title>ITALY: Fiat closes sharply firmer on Milan Bourse.</title>
<headline>Fiat closes sharply firmer on Milan Bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fiat SpA shares firmed strongly in late trade on the Milan stock market after recent session losses, closing 5.59 percent up at 4,195 lire just off its day's high of 4,200 lire, in fair volume of 6.8 million shares.</p>
<p>Traders said Fiat and other blue chip stocks were beginning &quot;to breathe again&quot; after being neglected amid heavy buying of energy group ENI in its recent second tranche share sale.</p>
<p>Also helping was the recent billion dollar market debut of Fiat's New Holland NV  and market talk of restructuring in Fiat's chemical sector.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
